  "question": {
    "text": "You are asked to design a shaving mirror assuming that a person keeps it at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from his face and views the magnified image of the face at the closest comfortable distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The radius of curvature of the mirror would then be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0238_d6d8b4bbb365.png\" style=\"width: 310px; height: 205px;\" /><br /><br />If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is the position of the face of man then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math> is the position of the image of a face. As&nbsp;the image is formed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from the object.<math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> From concave mirror image is 15cm behind the mirror. So, <math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math>. So, the radius of curvature,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math>"
  }
}